        "predicate": "summary",
        "object": "<p>Hardware engineering executive succeeding Tim Cook is a longtime Apple insider, indicating company will continue strategy that has led to record profits</p><p>Tim Cook stepped down as CEO of Apple on 31 August. John Ternus, a longtime company veteran, succeeded him the next day as the company’s new chief executive. Cook has transitioned to the role of executive chairman of Apple’s board of directors.</p><p>Ternus, a hardware engineering executive, is a tenured Apple insider, and his ascension indicates the company will stay the course that has led to record profits under Cook’s leadership. Apple’s yearly profit now tops $100bn, the company is worth about $4.5tn, and it has notched record revenue from its iPhones this year, boosted by <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/jan/29/apple-ai-plans-siri-reboot\">renewed demand in China</a>.</p> <a href=\"https://www.theguardian.com/technology/2026/apr/20/john-ternus-apple-ceo-tim-cook\">Continue reading...</a>"
